- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ Whale sync client: passphrase-based sync encryption design confirmed to exist (vendor help statement "passphrase never sent to/stored on server" + per-device re-entry requirement + Android 3.8.6.2 "synchronization encryption" release note) → local key-storage/KDF analysis is a live class, and the vendor's claim itself is falsifiable via binary analysis
